{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779376002,"nonce":"NEcFR2Fhe/Cf8ZG0l/lhHnQtvIA=","message":"## Current state after `integration/studio-task-authoring-boundary`\n\nReopening this umbrella because the merged work did **not** resolve the main `ValueSpec` / expression-valued parameter design. It landed a bounded substrate slice and a deliberately narrow delayed-reach editor, not the generalized authoring system described in this issue.\n\nWhat landed:\n\n- Studio authoring ingress now normalizes runtime graph names into authoring names (`SimpleStagedNetwork` -\u003e `Network`, `target` -\u003e `input`) across frontend restore/open paths, backend project ingress, schema enumeration, provider validation, and worker preflight. This came from `0fcb25a` and is useful groundwork for task/value authoring.\n- The task panel writes delayed-reach timeline edits into `StudioScenarioSpec.task_spec` and refreshes `task_binding_spec` through the Task Data contract.\n- Delayed-reach epoch lengths are represented internally as structured `StudioValueSpec` constants with per-trial metadata.\n- Delayed-reach Task Data/value metadata now includes function-valued target generation for compact task params, aligned with the `TaskDataSchema` / `ValueSchema` substrate.\n- The startup placeholder tab behavior was fixed so the clean built-in `SimpleReaches` model does not persist beside the real saved Movement Ramp project.\n\nWhat was intentionally trimmed back before merge:\n\n- The redundant green-bar timeline preview was removed because it only duplicated the checkbox table and did not add authoring power.\n- `movement_target` was removed from the model-input signal table; it remains protocol/loss target data and should not look like another graph input lane.\n- Epoch columns are numbered again. The visible max length now reflects the actual possible sampled maximum while preserving the existing backend exclusive-upper-bound representation.\n\nWhat remains open here:\n\n- A real shared `ValueSpec` / expression system with modes for constants, references, expressions, reusable functions, distributions, and schedules.\n- Structured value editors/chips that let users construct values and functions, rather than just read explanatory text or toggle signal presence.\n- A project/function-template library for step, pulse, ramp, piecewise, interpolation, noise processes, target trajectories, perturbation profiles, etc.\n- Distribution authoring with explicit sampling scope and deterministic seed/manifest metadata.\n- A task timeline where non-boolean cells open structured value/function editors and where rows are backed by explicit signal/protocol definitions, not just hardcoded delayed-reach arrays.\n- Adoption of the same value editor for objective weights, eval overrides, component/acausal parameters, sweeps/replicates, and intervention profiles.\n- Backend lowering/validation for the above with structured spec-path errors.\n\nDesign note from the merged slice: the current table should be treated as scaffolding over the compact delayed-reach params, not as the final task authoring model. The next serious child issue should probably start from the shared value/function/distribution editor and then reuse it in task timelines and objectives, rather than further polishing the checkbox table.","files":null}]}